<title>BELGIUM: UK's Clarke unsure of progress on EMU budget pact.</title>
<headline>UK's Clarke unsure of progress on EMU budget pact.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Monday he was uncertain over how much progress European Union finance ministers would make on a budget pact for countries inside monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm not sure whether we will reach agreement today,&quot; Clarke told journalists ahead of a meeting of the bloc's 15 ministers.</p>
<p>Agreement on a budget stability pact that would fine countries running excessive deficits inside economic and monetary union has remained elusive due to renewed Germany demands for stricter rules.</p>
<p>- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
